data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:37:17.956695+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_8762a5d278bc47b6", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_57ac84d71ca3", "workspace_id": "ws_22a00fecef95", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "span_id": "sem_8762a5d278bc47b6", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert geospatial produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:37:17.928766+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "geospatial"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "main"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "geospatial", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'geospatial'.", "answer": "Resolved region: Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\n\n**Center coordinates:** 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W\n\n**Search radius:** 100 km (conservative default for regional GNSS and seismic analysis; no explicit radius specified in request)\n\n**Bounding box (OSM):** [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306] (min_lon, min_lat, max_lon, max_lat)\n\n**Provenance:** OpenStreetMap Nominatim (osm_nominatim) \u2014 grounded geocoding service lookup\n\n**Confidence:** High (administrative-level boundary match with OSM importance score 0.84)\n\n**Status:** Resolved and ready for downstream data discovery and event analysis", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [{"name": "geo_geocode", "args": {"query": "Los Angeles", "countrycodes": "us", "limit": 1}, "ok": true, "telemetry_source": "agent_trajectory", "result": "[{'display_name': 'Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States', 'lat': 34.0536909, 'lon': -118.242766, 'bbox': [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], 'type': 'administrative', 'importance': 0.8410828881088647, 'provenance': 'osm_nominatim'}]"}, {"name": "finish", "args": {}, "ok": true, "telemetry_source": "agent_trajectory", "result": "Completed."}, {"name": "clio_prior_workflow_state", "args": {}, "ok": true, "telemetry_source": "blueprint_react_context_seed"}, {"name": "geo_geocode", "args": {"query": "Los Angeles", "countrycodes": "us", "limit": 1}, "ok": true, "duration_ms": 778.2125830126461, "telemetry_source": "blueprint_react_tool_wrapper", "result": "[{'display_name': 'Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States', 'lat': 34.0536909, 'lon': -118.242766, 'bbox': [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], 'type': 'administrative', 'importance': 0.8410828881088647, 'provenance': 'osm_nominatim'}]"}], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "trajectory": {"thought_0": "The request asks me to resolve \"Los Angeles\" to grounded coordinates and region definition. The question provides a place name (\"Los Angeles\") but not explicit coordinates, so I need to call the `geo_geocode` tool to look up this location in OpenStreetMap Nominatim. This will provide real, grounded latitude/longitude coordinates, a bounding box, and verifiable provenance. I'll restrict the search to the US using `countrycodes=\"us\"` to ensure we get Los Angeles, California rather than any other place with that name.", "tool_name_0": "geo_geocode", "tool_args_0": {"query": "Los Angeles", "countrycodes": "us", "limit": 1}, "observation_0": "[{'display_name': 'Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States', 'lat': 34.0536909, 'lon': -118.242766, 'bbox': [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], 'type': 'administrative', 'importance': 0.8410828881088647, 'provenance': 'osm_nominatim'}]", "thought_1": "The geo_geocode tool has successfully resolved \"Los Angeles\" to real coordinates from OpenStreetMap Nominatim. The result provides:\n\n- **Center coordinates**: 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W\n- **Bounding box**: [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306] (min_lon, min_lat, max_lon, max_lat)\n- **Region name**: Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\n- **Provenance**: osm_nominatim (grounded OpenStreetMap lookup)\n- **Confidence**: High (administrative boundary match with importance=0.84)\n\nThe request did not specify a search radius, so I am adopting a conservative default of **100 km** for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event catalog queries. This radius captures the greater Los Angeles metropolitan area, surrounding seismic zones, and relevant EarthScope/NDP station networks while maintaining appropriate geographic scope.\n\nGeospatial resolution is now complete. The resolved region (center, bbox, radius, and high-confidence provenance) is ready for downstream data discovery and seismic event retrieval.", "tool_name_1": "finish", "tool_args_1": {}, "observation_1": "Completed."}, "reasoning": "The user requested resolution of \"Los Angeles\" to grounded coordinates and region definition suitable for EarthScope/NDP GNSS station discovery and seismic event catalog queries. Since the request provided a place name without explicit coordinates, I invoked the `geo_geocode` tool with query=\"Los Angeles\" and countrycodes=\"us\" to retrieve a verified, grounded lookup from OpenStreetMap Nominatim. The tool returned the administrative boundary for Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California with center coordinates 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W and a bounding box spanning [\u2212118.668\u00b0W, 33.660\u00b0N, \u2212118.155\u00b0W, 34.337\u00b0N]. The request did not specify a search radius, so I applied a conservative default of 100 km, which captures the greater Los Angeles metropolitan area and surrounding seismic zones while maintaining appropriate geographic scope for regional analysis. This region is now ready for downstream data discovery and seismic event retrieval."}}}

