data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:40:45.744673+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_3b08fe86c20746bd", "event_type": "expert.lifecycle.started", "session_id": "sess_57ac84d71ca3", "workspace_id": "ws_22a00fecef95", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "span_id": "sem_3b08fe86c20746bd", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "running", "summary": "expert ndp_resource_resolver started", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:40:45.729105+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "ndp_resource_resolver", "role": "expert"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {}, "provider": {}, "payload": {"expert_id": "ndp_resource_resolver", "expert_span_id": "1f1673e630ab4282", "input": {"question": "Stage the time-series CSV for the top-ranked EarthScope station candidate MTA1 (0.3 km from Los Angeles center) and provide fallback options if MTA1 is unavailable. Search NDP for the station-specific time-series resource and stage the CSV with columns including time, east, north, and up displacement components. Required columns: time, east, north, up. Fallback candidates (in order of proximity): PKRD (2.2 km), ELSC (4.1 km), USC2 (5.0 km), SILK (5.8 km).\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n(Delegating to ndp_resource_resolver for station time-series CSV staging; no final answer yet.)\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": false, \"metadata_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"status\": \"metadata_only\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"completed_stages\": [\"geospatial\"], \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 100, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"warnings\": [\"Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request\"]}, \"orchestrator_step\": \"delegating_to_data\", \"request_type\": \"full_pipeline\", \"station_catalog\": {\"candidate_count\": 155, \"station_ids\": [\"MTA1\", \"PKRD\", \"ELSC\", \"USC2\", \"SILK\", \"OXYC\", \"P800\", \"LEE2\", \"LEEP\", \"GVRS\", \"BGIS\", \"NOPK\", \"MHMS\", \"VDCY\", \"CIT1\", \"MILK\", \"BRAN\", \"P799\", \"HOLP\", \"LFRS\", \"DYH2\", \"WNRA\", \"BKMS\", \"JPLM\", \"FCTF\", \"UCLP\", \"WRHS\", \"RHCL\", \"WHC1\", \"CSDH\", \"RHCG\", \"LONG\", \"CRHS\", \"WLSN\", \"VIMT\", \"LBC1\", \"LPHS\", \"WMAP\", \"TORP\", \"LBCH\", \"LBC2\", \"HBCO\", \"WCHS\", \"CVHS\", \"PVRS\", \"SNHS\", \"PVHS\", \"AZU1\", \"CGDM\", \"LAPC\", \"CSN1\", \"DAM3\", \"DAM2\", \"BLSA\", \"VNCX\", \"P517\", \"P587\", \"CMP9\", \"CBHS\", \"SPMS\", \"CHIL\", \"SPK1\", \"PVE3\", \"VTIS\", \"PSDM\", \"CCCS\", \"ROCK\", \"LORS\", \"SACY\", \"SKYB\", \"TWMS\", \"CLAR\", \"VNPS\", \"JNHG\", \"FVPK\", \"DVPB\", \"ELLY\", \"CJVG\", \"OEOC\", \"LRRG\", \"HOL3\", \"PBPP\", \"TOST\", \"LL01\", \"CTDM\", \"P574\", \"CNPP\", \"TRAK\", \"TABL\", \"LGWD\", \"NOCO\", \"QHTP\", \"CIRX\", \"MPWD\", \"P561\", \"SFDM\", \"EWPP\", \"P575\", \"FMVT\", \"LINJ\", \"P581\", \"WHYT\", \"LLAS\", \"LPCG\", \"CAT3\", \"THMS\", \"THM2\", \"FMTP\", \"RKMG\", \"WKPK\", \"ELTN\", \"MJPK\", \"CSCI\", \"CHMS\", \"FOXG\", \"CJMS\", \"BRPK\", \"SBCC\", \"MAT2\", \"LMSG\", \"CJMG\", \"GHRP\", \"KBRC\", \"SOMT\", \"P555\", \"P729\", \"RTHS\", \"CAT2\", \"P556\", \"P471\", \"LMHG\", \"MLFP\", \"P612\", \"ELSG\", \"OVLS\", \"HIVI\", \"ECFS\", \"P577\", \"RMVJ\", \"P560\", \"P470\", \"P582\", \"RCSC\", \"RSTP\", \"TPOG\", \"P808\", \"VNCO\", \"ALPP\", \"NH...", "system_prompt": "# NDP Resource Resolver Expert\n\nYou stage the actual GNSS time-series CSV(s) \u2014 the step that turns \"we found candidate\nstations\" into \"we have analysis-ready data.\" Stage the station(s) the request needs:\nthe single nearest by default, or the several it asked to compare. You MUST call the\ntools; do not finish without staging (unless there are no candidates \u2014 see below).\n\n## No in-region candidates \u2192 stage nothing (honest no-coverage)\n\nIf `station_catalog.status=no_candidates` or `station_catalog.station_ids` is empty,\nthe region has no EarthScope GNSS coverage. Do NOT search or stage anything, do NOT\ninvent a station. Emit `acquisition.status=missing`, `analysis_ready=false` with a\nshort no-coverage note, and finish.\n\n## When there ARE candidates \u2014 actually stage the CSV(s)\n\nYou HAVE the tools \u2014 CALL them. Do NOT emit a plan, a `preferred_calls` list, or\n`status=\"search_required\"` describing calls you *would* make. While candidates exist,\n`metadata_only` / `missing` / `search_required` are NOT valid final results \u2014 they mean\nyou stopped before staging.\n\nWalk `station_catalog.station_ids` in ranked order. For EACH station you stage:\n\n1. **Search** its datasets: `ndp_search_datasets` with the id in `dataset_title` (NOT\n   `resource_name`, which 502s): `{ \"dataset_title\": \"<station id>\", \"limit\": 20 }` \u2014\n   one station per call.\n2. **Pick the CSV url**: choose the dataset whose `resources` has a `.csv` named like\n   `<station id>.*.csv` (a per-station time series, e.g. `P475.CI.LY_.20.csv`) and read\n   that resource's real https `url`. That is the time series, NOT the metadata catalog.\n3. **Stage by url**: `ndp_stage_resource` with `url` = that .csv url and\n   `max_bytes=60000000` (a station CSV exceeds the default). Do NOT pass `output_dir`.\n4. **Record it** from the `ndp_stage_resource` result, copying paths byte-for-byte\n   (never invent or reconstruct a path): set `acquisition.local_path` to the returned\n   `local_path` (the first staged station), plus `acquisition.source_url`,\n   `acquisition.size_bytes`, `acquisition.status=\"staged\"`, `analysis_ready=true`,\n   `required_columns=[\"time\",\"east\",\"north\",\"up\"]`, and\n   `resource_candidate.station_id` = the id in that filename (`status=\"selected\"`,\n   `geographically_grounded=true`).\n\nIf a station's search finds no `.csv`, or staging fails, skip it and move to the next\nranked id \u2014 never widen beyond the ranked list, never invent a path. Keep going until\nyou have staged as many stations as the request asked for (most often just one). When\nyou stage several, collect every staged CSV path in `acquisition.local_paths` (ranked\norder) so the visualization expert can overlay them. You are done once the requested\nstation(s) are staged; a `blocked` state is valid only after you actually tried the\nranked stations and none staged.\n\nThe station id in `resource_candidate.station_id`, in each staged path's filename, and\nthe CSV you staged must match. Never stage the metadata catalog\n(`earthscope_converted_data.csv` / the cleaned `Site,Latitude,Longitude` file) as the\nanalysis CSV \u2014 that is station metadata, not a time series.\n\nActive workspace root: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws\nWrite generated artifacts (files, charts, exports) inside the active workspace root using absolute paths so they stay with the session. Read inputs from wherever the user points you.\nWrites are only permitted under: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws, /tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run."}}}}

