data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:42:11.579128+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_5787f6a2c3284dbe", "event_type": "blueprint.delegation.completed", "session_id": "sess_57ac84d71ca3", "workspace_id": "ws_22a00fecef95", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "span_id": "sem_5787f6a2c3284dbe", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "data returned a compact result to main.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:42:11.562010+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "data", "role": "child_expert"}, "subject": {"agent_id": "main", "role": "parent_expert"}, "blueprint": {"pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "main", "child_expert": "data"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"delegate_to": "data", "agent_id": "data", "question": "Discover and rank EarthScope/NDP GNSS stations within the Los Angeles region (center 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, radius 100 km). Identify candidate stations suitable for analyzing regional ground deformation and providing station context for seismic activity analysis. Stage a time-series CSV from a suitable candidate station if available, with columns including time, east, north, and up displacement.", "status": "completed", "execute": true, "source": "agent_next_expert", "parent_id": "main", "pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "provider_id": "", "model_id": "", "fallback_warnings": [], "stage": "delegate.completed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "return_to": "main", "depth": 0, "duration_ms": 16694, "execution_mode": "blueprint_chain_of_thought", "input": "Discover and rank EarthScope/NDP GNSS stations within the Los Angeles region (center 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, radius 100 km). Identify candidate stations suitable for analyzing regional ground deformation and providing station context for seismic activity analysis. Stage a time-series CSV from a suitable candidate station if available, with columns including time, east, north, and up displacement.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n(Delegating to data expert for station discovery; no final answer yet.)\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"completed_stages\": [\"geospatial\"], \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 100, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"warnings\": [\"Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request\"]}, \"orchestrator_step\": \"delegating_to_data\", \"request_type\": \"full_pipeline\", \"user_request_summary\": \"Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact\"}}", "output": "**Data Acquisition Complete: MTA1 GNSS Time-Series Successfully Staged for Los Angeles Region**\n\n## Summary\n\nEarthScope GNSS data acquisition for the Los Angeles region (center 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, radius 100 km) has been completed successfully.\n\n### Resolved Region\n- **Location**: Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\n- **Center**: 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W\n- **Search radius**: 100 km\n- **Coverage**: High-confidence geospatial resolution from OpenStreetMap Nominatim\n\n### Station Discovery & Selection\n- **Stations identified**: 155 EarthScope/GNSS stations within the region\n- **Top candidate selected**: **MTA1** (0.3 km from region center \u2014 nearly at center)\n- **Station ranking**: All 155 stations ranked by proximity; MTA1 chosen as closest and most representative of the central LA area\n- **Regional coverage**: Dense clustering near city center with strong distribution across greater LA basin to 100 km radius\n\n### Staged Time-Series Data\n- **File path**: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- **Source URL**: `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- **File size**: 50,424,246 bytes (~50.4 MB)\n- **Content type**: CSV (text/csv)\n- **Data period**: 2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12\n- **Station ID**: MTA1\n- **Status**: Analysis-ready and validated\n\n### Data Availability\nThe MTA1 station provides three-dimensional GNSS time-series data suitable for regional ground deformation analysis and seismic activity context. The staged CSV contains displacement components (east, north, up) with time indexing required for seismic-tectonic interpretation.", "workflow_state": {"completed_stages": ["geospatial"], "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "orchestrator_step": "delegating_to_data", "request_type": "full_pipeline", "user_request_summary": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact", "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "acquisition": {"status": "staged", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525