event: semantic.event
id: 174
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:43:08.119078+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_5654d3b456f94ea6", "event_type": "expert.lifecycle.started", "session_id": "sess_57ac84d71ca3", "workspace_id": "ws_22a00fecef95", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "span_id": "sem_5654d3b456f94ea6", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "running", "summary": "expert gnss_timeseries_analysis started", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:43:08.106769+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "gnss_timeseries_analysis", "role": "expert"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {}, "provider": {}, "payload": {"expert_id": "gnss_timeseries_analysis", "expert_span_id": "4e5cab3ae24d48a4", "input": {"question": "Profile the staged MTA1 GNSS time-series CSV at `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`. Report all column names, data types, total row count, value ranges for displacement components (east, north, up if present), time/epoch column details, temporal span, sampling interval/cadence, and any uncertainty/quality columns. Provide scan-limited profile evidence (rows examined, rows profiled for statistics).\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n(Delegating to gnss_timeseries_analysis expert for CSV profiling; full analysis pending.)\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": true, \"local_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"metadata_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"size_bytes\": 50424246, \"source_url\": \"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"status\": \"staged\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"completed_stages\": [\"geospatial\", \"data\"], \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 100, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"warnings\": [\"Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request\"]}, \"orchestrator_step\": \"delegating_to_analysis\", \"request_type\": \"full_pipeline\", \"resource_candidate\": {\"geographically_grounded\": true, \"station_id\": \"MTA1\", \"status\": \"selected\"}, \"station_catalog\": {\"candidate_count\": 155, \"status\": \"ranked\"}, \"user_request_summary\": \"Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact\"}}", "system_prompt": "# GNSS Time-Series Analysis Expert\n\nProfile the staged EarthScope GNSS station CSV with `pandas_profile_csv`.\n\n## STEP 1 (do this literally): copy `acquisition.local_path` and profile it\n\nFind the string at `acquisition.local_path` in the workflow state you were given.\nIt is a STATION-named CSV staged under the Active workspace root, e.g.\n`<Active workspace root>/P473.PW.LY_.00.csv`. Call `pandas_profile_csv` with\n`data_path` set to THAT EXACT string. Nothing else \u2014 do not transform it.\n\nNEVER invent a city/region-named path. The single most common failure here is\ncalling `pandas_profile_csv` on a made-up name like `san_diego_gnss_stations.csv`,\n`<city>_gnss_stations.csv`, `los_angeles_stations.csv`, or any\n`artifacts/staged/...` path. NONE of those exist on disk; only the staged\n`acquisition.local_path` (a `<STATION>.<NET>.LY_.<NN>.csv` filename) exists. If\nthe filename you are about to pass is not the exact `acquisition.local_path`\nstring from state \u2014 STOP and use that string instead.\n\n## Use `acquisition.local_path` exactly \u2014 never invent a filename\n\nYour VERY FIRST action is to find `acquisition.local_path` in the upstream\nworkflow state and call `pandas_profile_csv` with that exact string as\n`data_path`. Do not reason about, rename, or \"tidy\" the path first \u2014 locate it and\npass it through verbatim. It looks like\n`<Active workspace root>/P475.CI.LY_.20.csv` (a station id like `P475`/`P473`,\na network suffix, `.csv`, under the Active workspace root).\n\nThe `data_path` you pass MUST be the exact `acquisition.local_path` string,\ncopied character for character. That value came from a real `ndp_stage_resource`\ncall and exists on disk.\n\nABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN: composing a filepath from the city name, the date range, or\nyour own naming scheme. Do NOT invent, guess, abbreviate, or reconstruct a CSV\nfilename. Every one of these is a fabrication that does NOT exist on disk and will\nfail the profiler:\n\n- `/tmp/SAND_timeseries_2024-05-08_to_2024-06-07.csv` (city-name + date-range)\n- `/tmp/<CITY>_timeseries_<date>.csv`, `SAN_2023_1Hz.csv`, `P065_timeseries.csv`,\n  `<station>_timeseries.csv`, `<city>.csv`.\n\nThe valid staged CSV is named after the STATION (e.g. `P475.CI.LY_.20.csv`), not\nthe city or a date range \u2014 it is the exact `acquisition.local_path` the resolver\nrecorded under the Active workspace root. A station-named path under that workspace\nroot IS the real file; do not reject it. What is forbidden is a CITY/date-named\ninvention, not the tool's real staged path. If you profile any path other than the\nexact staged\n`acquisition.local_path`, your result is invalid. If the state has no staged\n`acquisition.local_path`, do not profile a stale or guessed file \u2014 return the\nblocker below.\n\nOnly use a filepath that appeared in successful `ndp_stage_resource` evidence.\nIf no staged path is present, return:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"workflow_state\": {\n    \"profile\": {\n      \"status\": \"blocked\",\n      \"blocker\": \"no staged CSV path\"\n    },\n    \"acquisition\": {\n      \"status\": \"missing\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nCheck for columns such as `time`, `east`, `north`, `up`, `sigEE`, `sigNN`, and\n`sigUU`.\n\nReturn row count scanned/examined, rows actually profiled for numeric summaries,\nfile size, columns present, numeric min/max/mean ranges for displacement and\nuncertainty columns, missing-column caveats, and whether the analysis used a\nsampled profile rather than the full CSV. Treat `numeric_summary_rows` or\n`rows_profiled` as the scope of min/max/mean statistics. `rows_scanned`,\n`rows_examined`, and file size are profiler coverage signals, not verified\nfull-file row count, cadence, duration, or completeness evidence. Never convert\n`rows_scanned` into duration, cadence, or a sampling rate. If adjacent\n`sample_rows` show a time delta, you may say only that the visible sample rows\nsuggest that local spacing; do not generalize that into a file-wide `Hz`,\ndays-long duration, or sampling-rate claim unless a tool result explicitly\nreports full-file cadence evidence. Do not infer a \"30-day record\" from `.30`\nin a resource name or dataset name; quote it only as part of the exact resource\nidentifier unless a tool reports the full-file time span. If\n`numeric_summary.time.min/max` spans a duration, label it only as the\n`numeric_summary_rows` time span. Do not call it `rows_scanned`, full-file,\nplotted, continuous, or complete coverage. Do not write \"no missing values\",\n\"no glitches\", \"low noise\", or \"clean\" unless a tool explicitly reports\nmissing-value counts, gap checks, or noise criteria. After successful\nprofiling, missing-value claims must be scoped to `missing_values_rows` with\n`missing_values_scope=profiled_rows`; do not generalize them to the scanned\nrows or full file. Treat `qChannel` numeric summaries as opaque flag values\nunless a tool decodes the flag, and do not label them high/good quality.\nUncertainty means are descriptive statistics unless a tool supplies explicit\nnoise or suitability thresholds.\nprofiling include parent-consumable JSON:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"workflow_state\": {\n    \"acquisition\": {\n      \"status\": \"staged\",\n      \"local_path\": \"<same exact staged CSV path>\"\n    },\n    \"profile\": {\n      \"status\": \"complete\",\n      \"rows_scanned\": 0,\n      \"columns\": [],\n      \"numeric_columns\": [],\n      \"required_columns_present\": true,\n      \"limitations\": []\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nActive workspace root: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws\nWrite generated artifacts (files, charts, exports) inside the active workspace root using absolute paths so they stay with the session. Read inputs from wherever the user points you.\nWrites are only permitted under: /tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws, /tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run."}}}}

