nitoring and seismic event station correlation are present.\n\n**Data Quality (Scan-Limited Profile):**\nUncertainty ranges from the profiled 5,000-row sample indicate:\n- Horizontal positioning uncertainty: 3.3 cm (sigEE/sigNN means)\n- Vertical positioning uncertainty: 6.5 cm (sigUU mean)\n\nThese centimeter-scale uncertainties are consistent with high-rate EarthScope GNSS observations. Null-value count in profiled rows: zero.\n\n**Important Limitation:**\nProfile evidence is scan-limited (5,000 of 250,000 rows). Full-file cadence, duration, temporal continuity, and complete data-quality statistics were not verified. Complete-record suitability assessment requires full-file analysis.\n\n**Network Context:**\nMTA1 is the closest of 155 ranked EarthScope stations in the region. Secondary candidates (PKRD at 2.2 km, ELSC at 4.1 km, USC2 at 5.0 km, SILK at 5.8 km) provide network redundancy and multi-station monitoring potential.\n\n**Station Selection & Recommendations:**\n- **Single-station sufficiency**: MTA1's central location and complete data structure support initial regional deformation context and seismic event station metadata. A single station at the region center is a reasonable first-order choice for exploratory analysis.\n- **Multi-station option**: The 155-station network enables cross-validation or multi-station strain/rotation analysis if the user's analysis scope expands.\n- **Data qualification**: Preliminary suitability for regional monitoring is supported by geographic position and column presence. Full-record suitability requires verification of cadence, continuity, and temporal coverage.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "completed_stages": ["geospatial", "data"], "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "orchestrator_step": "delegating_to_analysis", "profile": {"path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "scan_limited": true, "status": "complete"}, "request_type": "full_pipeline", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected"}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 155, "status": "ranked"}, "user_request_summary": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact", "network_analysis": {"assessment": "MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence/duration not verified.", "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "preliminary_suitability_confirmed", "network_context": "155 ranked stations available; MTA1 is closest; fallback stations (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km) enable multi-station analysis if needed"}}}}}

