event: semantic.event
id: 215
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:45:02.182489+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_7847f7e02e2e4367", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_57ac84d71ca3", "workspace_id": "ws_22a00fecef95", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "span_id": "sem_7847f7e02e2e4367", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert analysis produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:45:02.172195+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "analysis"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "main"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "analysis", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'analysis'.", "answer": "(Delegating to seismic_event_catalog for earthquake/seismic event evidence; full analysis and synthesis pending.)", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "The analysis orchestrator has successfully completed both required child analysis steps:\n1. \u2713 `gnss_timeseries_analysis`: Profiled the staged MTA1 CSV with all required columns and uncertainty metrics\n2. \u2713 `station_network_analysis`: Assessed MTA1's suitability as geographically optimal at the LA region center\n\n**Optional next step evaluation:**\nThe user's broader request explicitly asks to \"Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles\" and \"find public EarthScope or earthquake catalog evidence\" and \"analyze the events and station context.\" This satisfies the criterion: \"Request `seismic_event_catalog` only when the user explicitly asks for earthquakes, event catalogs, magnitudes, depths, epicenters...\"\n\nThe user explicitly requested:\n- \"recent seismic activity\"\n- \"earthquake catalog evidence\"\n- \"analyze the events\"\n\nTherefore, the `seismic_event_catalog` child should be invoked to fulfill this explicit aspect of the request. This will provide event context to complement the staged GNSS data and support the full analysis pipeline before visualization and synthesis."}}}

