event: message.part.delta
id: 221
data: {"type": "message.part.delta", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:45:21.897250+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "message_id": "msg_asst_b3567fb7ada5", "part_id": "part_260b5b975b19", "stream_source": "live", "delta": {"text_append": "**Seismic Event Catalog Capability Gap**\n\nThis analysis pack does not have a live earthquake event-catalog tool available for querying USGS, IRIS, or equivalent seismic databases. Therefore, the requested event-context evidence cannot be retrieved.\n\n**What is missing:**\nTo complete the event-context layer for the Los Angeles region (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, \u00b1100 km radius) during the December 3, 2024 time window, the workflow would require:\n- **USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API** or equivalent live event catalog query tool\n- **Event filtering by region, magnitude threshold, and date range**\n- **Magnitude, depth, epicenter coordinates, and temporal event data**\n- **Event-to-station distance calculations for MTA1 and network context**\n\n**Impact on Analysis:**\nWithout live event-catalog access, the synthesis cannot provide:\n- Recent seismic activity counts and magnitudes for the LA region\n- Event timing and epicenter context for GNSS displacement interpretation\n- Cross-correlation of GNSS observations with known seismic events\n- Event-driven deformation attribution\n\nThe staged MTA1 GNSS time-series and station network analysis remain complete and valid. Seismic event correlation would require a separate event-catalog query tool.\n\n"}}}

event: semantic.event
id: 222
data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:45:21.936192+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_4a54abc8c90841f3", "event_type": "expert.response.completed", "session_id": "sess_57ac84d71ca3", "workspace_id": "ws_22a00fecef95", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "span_id": "sem_4a54abc8c90841f3", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "Expert seismic_event_catalog produced a response.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:45:21.925549+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "seismic_event_catalog"}, "subject": {}, "blueprint": {"agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "analysis"}, "provider": {"provider_id": "", "model_id": ""}, "payload": {"selected_expert": "seismic_event_catalog", "route_source": "agent_blueprint", "route_reason": "Session selected Agent Blueprint expert 'seismic_event_catalog'.", "answer": "**Seismic Event Catalog Capability Gap**\n\nThis analysis pack does not have a live earthquake event-catalog tool available for querying USGS, IRIS, or equivalent seismic databases. Therefore, the requested event-context evidence cannot be retrieved.\n\n**What is missing:**\nTo complete the event-context layer for the Los Angeles region (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, \u00b1100 km radius) during the December 3, 2024 time window, the workflow would require:\n- **USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API** or equivalent live event catalog query tool\n- **Event filtering by region, magnitude threshold, and date range**\n- **Magnitude, depth, epicenter coordinates, and temporal event data**\n- **Event-to-station distance calculations for MTA1 and network context**\n\n**Impact on Analysis:**\nWithout live event-catalog access, the synthesis cannot provide:\n- Recent seismic activity counts and magnitudes for the LA region\n- Event timing and epicenter context for GNSS displacement interpretation\n- Cross-correlation of GNSS observations with known seismic events\n- Event-driven deformation attribution\n\nThe staged MTA1 GNSS time-series and station network analysis remain complete and valid. Seismic event correlation would require a separate event-catalog query tool.", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "The seismic_event_catalog expert has been requested to provide earthquake and seismic event evidence for the Los Angeles region (center 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, radius 100 km) during the time period of the staged MTA1 GNSS data (December 3, 2024, profiled temporal sample).\n\n**Capability Assessment:**\nThe system prompt explicitly states: \"This pack currently has no dedicated USGS event-catalog tool.\" The seismic_event_catalog expert has no live earthquake catalog tools available to query USGS, IRIS, or equivalent event databases for:\n- Recent earthquake magnitudes and depths\n- Epicenter locations within the LA region\n- Event temporal patterns\n- Event-to-station distance relationships\n\n**Honest Blocker:**\nAbsence of a live event-catalog tool prevents event-context analysis. This is not evidence that no events occurred in the LA region during the profiled time window; it is a tool/capability gap.\n\nPer system prompt guidance, the expert cannot and must not invent earthquake counts, magnitudes, dates, or event-catalog status claims."}}}

