und deformation monitoring, event-station distance relationships, and interpretation of GNSS displacement patterns in relation to tectonic activity.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n(Delegating to seismic_event_catalog for earthquake/seismic event evidence; full analysis and synthesis pending.)\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": true, \"local_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"metadata_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"size_bytes\": 50424246, \"source_url\": \"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"status\": \"staged\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"completed_stages\": [\"geospatial\", \"data\"], \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 100, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"warnings\": [\"Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request\"]}, \"network_analysis\": {\"assessment\": \"MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence/duration not verified.\", \"network_context\": \"155 ranked stations available; MTA1 is closest; fallback stations (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km) enable multi-station analysis if needed\", \"station_id\": \"MTA1\", \"status\": \"preliminary_suitability_confirmed\"}, \"orchestrator_step\": \"delegating_to_analysis\", \"profile\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"scan_limited\": true, \"status\": \"complete\"}, \"request_type\": \"full_pipeline\", \"resource_candidate\": {\"geographically_grounded\": true, \"station_id\": \"MTA1\", \"status\": \"selected\"}, \"station_catalog\": {\"candidate_count\": 155, \"status\": \"ranked\"}, \"user_request_summary\": \"Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography...", "output": "**Seismic Event Catalog Capability Gap**\n\nThis analysis pack does not have a live earthquake event-catalog tool available for querying USGS, IRIS, or equivalent seismic databases. Therefore, the requested event-context evidence cannot be retrieved.\n\n**What is missing:**\nTo complete the event-context layer for the Los Angeles region (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, \u00b1100 km radius) during the December 3, 2024 time window, the workflow would require:\n- **USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API** or equivalent live event catalog query tool\n- **Event filtering by region, magnitude threshold, and date range**\n- **Magnitude, depth, epicenter coordinates, and temporal event data**\n- **Event-to-station distance calculations for MTA1 and network context**\n\n**Impact on Analysis:**\nWithout live event-catalog access, the synthesis cannot provide:\n- Recent seismic activity counts and magnitudes for the LA region\n- Event timing and epicenter context for GNSS displacement interpretation\n- Cross-correlation of GNSS observations with known seismic events\n- Event-driven deformation attribution\n\nThe staged MTA1 GNSS time-series and station network analysis remain complete and valid. Seismic event correlation would require a separate event-catalog query tool.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "completed_stages": ["geospatial", "data"], "event_context": {"blocker": "no live event catalog tool available in this pack", "limitations": ["no_live_event_catalog_tool"], "next_action": "add or call a live earthquake/event catalog tool (e.g., USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API) for event counts, magnitudes, depths, and dates", "status": "blocked", "verified_event_count": null}, "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "network_analysis": {"assessment": "MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence/duration not verified.", "network_context": "155 ranked stations available; MTA1 is closest; fallback stations (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km) enable multi-station analysis if needed", "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "preliminary_suitability_confirmed"}, "orchestrator_step": "delegating_to_analysis", "profile": {"path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "scan_limited": true, "status": "complete"}, "request_type": "full_pipeline", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected"}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 155, "status": "ranked"}, "user_request_summary": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact"}, "tools_called": [], "children": [], "stream_source": "live"}, "agent_id": "analysis", "text": "analysis <- seismic_event_catalog", "parent_agent": "analysis", "child_agent": "seismic_event_catalog", "stage": "delegate.completed", "status": "completed"}}}

