data: {"type": "message.part.added", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:45:53.011006+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "message_id": "msg_asst_b3567fb7ada5", "stream_source": "live", "part": {"id": "live_handoff_e9eec0dfc074", "type": "expert_handoff", "metadata": {"delegate_to": "analysis", "agent_id": "analysis", "question": "Profile the staged MTA1 GNSS time-series CSV and assess station suitability for analyzing regional ground deformation and seismic activity. Examine temporal coverage, data completeness, and station location context relative to the Los Angeles region center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W). Report the time span, sampling characteristics, and any data quality observations relevant to seismic event correlation and deformation analysis.", "status": "completed", "execute": true, "source": "agent_next_expert", "parent_id": "main", "pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "provider_id": "", "model_id": "", "fallback_warnings": [], "stage": "delegate.completed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "return_to": "main", "depth": 0, "duration_ms": 20162, "execution_mode": "blueprint_chain_of_thought", "input": "Profile the staged MTA1 GNSS time-series CSV and assess station suitability for analyzing regional ground deformation and seismic activity. Examine temporal coverage, data completeness, and station location context relative to the Los Angeles region center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W). Report the time span, sampling characteristics, and any data quality observations relevant to seismic event correlation and deformation analysis.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n(Delegating to analysis expert for station profiling and suitability assessment; final answer pending.)\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": true, \"local_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"metadata_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"size_bytes\": 50424246, \"source_url\": \"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"status\": \"staged\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"completed_stages\": [\"geospatial\", \"data\"], \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 100, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"warnings\": [\"Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request\"]}, \"orchestrator_step\": \"delegating_to_analysis\", \"request_type\": \"full_pipeline\", \"resource_candidate\": {\"geographically_grounded\": true, \"station_id\": \"MTA1\", \"status\": \"selected\"}, \"station_catalog\": {\"candidate_count\": 155, \"station_ids\": [\"MTA1\", \"PKRD\", \"ELSC\", \"USC2\", \"SILK\", \"OXYC\", \"P800\", \"LEE2\", \"LEEP\", \"GVRS\", \"BGIS\", \"NOPK\", \"MHMS\", \"VDCY\", \"CIT1\", \"MILK\", \"BRAN\", \"P799\", \"HOLP\", \"LFRS\", \"DYH2\", \"WNRA\", \"BKMS\", \"JPLM\", \"FCTF\", \"UCLP\", \"WRHS\", \"RHCL\", \"WHC1\", \"CSDH\", \"RHCG\", \"LONG\", \"CRHS\", \"WLSN\", \"VIMT\", \"LBC1\", \"LPHS\", \"WMAP\", \"TORP\", \"LBCH\", \"LBC2\", \"HBCO\", \"WCHS\", \"CVHS\", \"PVRS\", \"SNHS\", \"PVHS\", \"AZU1\", \"CGDM\", \"LAPC\", \"CSN1\", \"DAM3\", \"DAM2\", \"BLSA\", \"VNCX\", \"P517\", \"P587\", \"CMP9\", \"CBHS\", \"SPMS\", \"CHIL\", \"SPK1\", \"PVE3\", \"VTIS\", \"PSDM\", \"CCCS\", \"ROCK\", \"LORS\", \"SACY\", \"SKYB\", \"TWMS\", \"CLAR\", \"VNPS\", \"JNHG\", \"FVPK\", \"DVPB\", \"ELLY\", \"CJVG\", \"OEOC\", \"LRRG\", \"HOL3\", \"PBPP\", \"TOST\", \"LL01\", \"CTDM\", \"P574\", \"CNPP\", \"TRAK\", \"TABL\", \"LGWD\", \"NOCO\", \"QHTP\", \"CIRX\", \"MPWD\", \"P561\", \"SFDM\", \"EWPP\", \"P575\", \"FMVT\", \"LINJ\", \"P581\", \"WHYT\", \"LLAS\",...", "output": "**MTA1 GNSS Station Analysis: Profile, Suitability, and Event-Context Summary**\n\n## GNSS Time-Series Profile\n\n**File & Data Structure:**\n- Staged CSV: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- Total rows: 250,000 | File size: 50.4 MB\n- All 8 required columns present: time (Unix ms), east, north, up (meters), sigEE, sigNN, sigUU (meters), qChannel (quality flag)\n\n**Displacement Ranges (profiled 5,000 rows):**\n- East: -0.07 to -0.03 m (mean: -0.047 m)\n- North: 0.029 to 0.058 m (mean: 0.045 m)\n- Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m (mean: 0.136 m)\n\n**Uncertainty Ranges (profiled 5,000 rows):**\n- Horizontal (sigEE/sigNN): 0.032\u20130.035 m (means: 3.3 cm)\n- Vertical (sigUU): 0.062\u20130.066 m (mean: 6.5 cm)\n\n**Temporal Coverage (profiled sample only):**\n- Time span: ~1.4 hours (December 3, 2024, 00:00\u201301:24 UTC)\n- Sample rows show 1000 ms increments (local 1 Hz sampling)\n- Null values in profiled rows: zero across all columns\n\n## Station Suitability Assessment\n\n**Geographic Position:**\nMTA1 is positioned 0.3 km from the Los Angeles region center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W), at the geographic heart of the analysis region. This central location is optimal for regional ground deformation monitoring.\n\n**Data Structure Fitness:**\nAll required GNSS analysis columns are present:\n- 3D displacement components (east, north, up)\n- 3D uncertainty components (sigEE, sigNN, sigUU)\n- Time reference for event correlation\n- Quality flag (qChannel, numeric, not decoded)\n\n**Preliminary Suitability Confirmation:**\nMTA1's central location and complete data structure support initial regional deformation context and seismic event station metadata analysis. A single station at the region center is a reasonable first-order choice for exploratory analysis.\n\n**Network Context:**\nMTA1 is the closest of 155 ranked EarthScope stations. Secondary candidates (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km, USC2 5.0 km, SILK 5.8 km) provide network redundancy and multi-station analysis options if scope expands.\n\n## Event-Context Capability Gap\n\n**Status:** Blocked \u2014 No live earthquake event-catalog tool available\n\nThe analysis pack lacks a live USGS/IRIS event-catalog query tool. Therefore, earthquake and seismic event evidence (magnitudes, depths, epicenter locations, temporal patterns) cannot be retrieved for the Los Angeles region.\n\n**Tools Needed for Complete Event Context:**\n- USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API or equivalent event-catalog service\n- Event filtering by region, magnitude, and date range\n- Event-to-station distance calculations for MTA1\n\n**Impact:** Without event-catalog access, the synthesis cannot cross-correlate GNSS observations with known seismic events or attribute deformation to specific earthquakes. The GNSS time-series and station analysis remain valid standalone evidence.\n\n## Critical Analysis Limitations\n\n**Scan-Limited Profile:**\nOnly 5,000 of 250,000 rows examined for statistics. Full-file cadence, duration, temporal continuity, and complete data-quality verification were not performed.\n\n**Unverified Full-File Characteristics:**\n- Full-file sampling cadence not confirmed (1 Hz observed in profiled sample)\n- Complete temporal span not verified\n- Missing-value status of full dataset not assessed\n- Quality flag (qChannel) not decoded\n\n**Conclusion:**\nPreliminary analysis of MTA1's suitability is supported by geographic position, column presence, and scan-limited uncertainty ranges. Complete suitability assessment and full-record quality verification require full-file analysis. Event-context correlation requires a live earthquake catalog tool.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "completed_stages": ["geospatial", "data"], "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "orchestrator_step": "delegating_to_analysis", "request_type": "full_pipeline", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected"}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 155, "status": "ranked"}, "user_request_summary": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact", "profile": {"status": "complete", "path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "scan_limited": true}, "network_analysis": {"assessment": "MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence/duration not verified.", "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "preliminary_suitability_confirmed", "network_context": "155 ranked stations available; MTA1 is closest; fallback stations (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km) enable multi-station analysis if needed"}, "event_context": {"blocker": "no live event catalog tool available in this pack", "limitations": ["no_live_event_catalog_tool"], "next_action": "add or call a live earthquake/event catalog tool (e.g., USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API) for event counts, magnitudes, depths, and dates", "status": "blocked", "verified_event_count": null}}, "tools_called": [{"call_id": "call_8bc0a9223c9d", "name": "pandas_profile_csv", "args": {"data_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "columns": null, "max_rows": null}, "ok": true, "duration_ms": 1192.577838897705, "cached": false, "telemetry_source": "live_observer", "result": "{\"success\": true, \"file_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"size_bytes\": 50424246, \"columns\": [\"time\", \"east\", \"north\", \"up\", \"sigEE\", \"sigNN\", \"sigUU\", \"qChannel\"], \"column_count\": 8, \"row_count\": 250000, \"rows_profiled\": 5000, \"row_scan_cap\": 250000, \"scan_limited\": true, \"profile_limited\": true, \"dtypes\": {\"time\": \"integer\", \"east\": \"float\", \"north\": \"float\", \"up\": \"float\", \"sigEE\": \"float\", \"sigNN\": \"float\", \"sigUU\": \"float\", \"qChannel\": \"integer\"}, \"null_counts\": {\"time\": 0, \"east\": 0, \"north\": 0, \"up\": 0, \"sigEE\": 0, \"sigNN\": 0, \"s