ement ranges: east -0.07 to -0.03 m, north 0.029 to 0.058 m, up 0.051 to 0.224 m; uncertainties: sigEE/sigNN ~3.3 cm, sigUU ~6.5 cm; scan-limited profile of 5000 rows). Consider station location at 0.3 km from LA region center and the 155-station network context.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n(Delegating to station_network_analysis for station suitability assessment; full analysis pending.)\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": true, \"local_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"metadata_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"size_bytes\": 50424246, \"source_url\": \"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"status\": \"staged\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"completed_stages\": [\"geospatial\", \"data\"], \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 100, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"warnings\": [\"Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request\"]}, \"orchestrator_step\": \"delegating_to_analysis\", \"profile\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"scan_limited\": true, \"status\": \"complete\"}, \"request_type\": \"full_pipeline\", \"resource_candidate\": {\"geographically_grounded\": true, \"station_id\": \"MTA1\", \"status\": \"selected\"}, \"station_catalog\": {\"candidate_count\": 155, \"status\": \"ranked\"}, \"user_request_summary\": \"Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact\"}}", "output": "**MTA1 Station Network Suitability Assessment for Los Angeles Region**\n\n**Geographic Position:**\nMTA1 is ideally located at 0.3 km from the Los Angeles region center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W), positioning it at the geographic heart of the analysis region. This central location provides optimal sensitivity to regional ground deformation patterns and seismic station context.\n\n**Data Structure Suitability:**\nThe staged MTA1 CSV contains all required GNSS analysis columns:\n- **Displacement components**: east, north, up (meters)\n- **Uncertainty components**: sigEE, sigNN, sigUU (meters)\n- **Time reference**: Unix milliseconds for event correlation\n- **Quality flag**: qChannel (numeric, not decoded)\n\nAll columns necessary for displacement-based deformation monitoring and seismic event station correlation are present.\n\n**Data Quality (Scan-Limited Profile):**\nUncertainty ranges from the profiled 5,000-row sample indicate:\n- Horizontal positioning uncertainty: 3.3 cm (sigEE/sigNN means)\n- Vertical positioning uncertainty: 6.5 cm (sigUU mean)\n\nThese centimeter-scale uncertainties are consistent with high-rate EarthScope GNSS observations. Null-value count in profiled rows: zero.\n\n**Important Limitation:**\nProfile evidence is scan-limited (5,000 of 250,000 rows). Full-file cadence, duration, temporal continuity, and complete data-quality statistics were not verified. Complete-record suitability assessment requires full-file analysis.\n\n**Network Context:**\nMTA1 is the closest of 155 ranked EarthScope stations in the region. Secondary candidates (PKRD at 2.2 km, ELSC at 4.1 km, USC2 at 5.0 km, SILK at 5.8 km) provide network redundancy and multi-station monitoring potential.\n\n**Station Selection & Recommendations:**\n- **Single-station sufficiency**: MTA1's central location and complete data structure support initial regional deformation context and seismic event station metadata. A single station at the region center is a reasonable first-order choice for exploratory analysis.\n- **Multi-station option**: The 155-station network enables cross-validation or multi-station strain/rotation analysis if the user's analysis scope expands.\n- **Data qualification**: Preliminary suitability for regional monitoring is supported by geographic position and column presence. Full-record suitability requires verification of cadence, continuity, and temporal coverage.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "completed_stages": ["geospatial", "data"], "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "orchestrator_step": "delegating_to_analysis", "profile": {"path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "scan_limited": true, "status": "complete"}, "request_type": "full_pipeline", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected"}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 155, "status": "ranked"}, "user_request_summary": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact", "network_analysis": {"assessment": "MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence/duration not verified.", "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "preliminary_suitability_confirmed", "network_context": "155 ranked stations available; MTA1 is closest; fallback stations (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km) enable multi-station analysis if needed"}}, "tools_called": [], "children": []}, {"agent_id": "analysis", "parent_id": "main", "dispatch_target": "analysis", "status": "completed", "stage": "parent.resumed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "resumed_from": "station_network_analysis", "depth": 0, "output": "**MTA1 Station Network Suitability Assessment for Los Angeles Region**\n\n**Geographic Position:**\nMTA1 is ideally located at 0.3 km from the Los Angeles region center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W), positioning it at the geographic heart of the analysis region. This central location provides optimal sensitivity to regional ground deformation patterns and seismic station context.\n\n**Data Structure Suitability:**\nThe staged MTA1 CSV contains all required GNSS analysis columns:\n- **Displacement components**: east, north, up (meters)\n- **Uncertainty components**: sigEE, sigNN, sigUU (meters)\n- **Time reference**: Unix milliseconds for event correlation\n- **Quality flag**: qChannel (numeric, not decoded)\n\nAll columns necessary for displacement-based deformation monitoring and seismic event station correlation are present.\n\n**Data Quality (Scan-Limited Profile):**\nUncertainty ranges from the profiled 5,000-row sample indicate:\n- Horizontal positioning uncertainty: 3.3 cm (sigEE/sigNN means)\n- Vertical positioning uncertainty: 6.5 cm (sigUU mean)\n\nThese centimeter-scale uncertainties are consistent with high-rate EarthScope GNSS observations. Null-value count in profiled rows: zero.\n\n**Important Limitation:**\nProfile evidence is scan-limited (5,000 of 250,000 rows). Full-file cadence, duration, temporal continuity, and complete data-quality statistics were not verified. Complete-record suitability assessment requires full-file analysis.\n\n**Network Context:**\nMTA1 is the closest of 155 ranked EarthScope stations in the region. Secondary candidates (PKRD at 2.2 km, ELSC at 4.1 km, USC2 at 5.0 km, SILK at 5.8 km) provide network redundancy and multi-station monitoring potential.\n\n**Station Selection & Recommendations:**\n- **Single-station sufficiency**: MTA1's central location and complete data structure support initial regional deformation context and seismic event station metadata. A single station at the region center is a reasonable first-order choice for exploratory analysis.\n- **Multi-station option**: The 155-station network enables cross-validation or multi-station strain/rotation analysis if the user's analysis scope expands.\n- **Data qualification**: Preliminary suitability for regional monitoring is supported by geographic position and column presence. Full-record suitability requires verification of cadence, continuity, and temporal coverage.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "completed_stages": ["geospatial", "data"], "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "orchestrator_step": "delegating_to_analysis", "profile": {"path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "scan_limited": true, "status": "complete"}, "request_type": "full_pipeline", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected"}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 155, "status": "ranked"}, "user_request_summary": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact", "network_analysis": {"assessment": "MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence/duration not verified.", "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "preliminary_suitability_confirmed", "network_context": "155 ranked stations available; MTA1 is closest; fallback stations (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km) enable multi-station analysis if needed"}}}, {"delegate_to": "seismic_event_catalog", "agent_id": "seismic_event_catalog", "question": "Search for recent earthquake and seismic event catalog evidence within the Los Angeles region (center 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, radius 100 km). Report available event magnitudes, depths, epicenter locations, and temporal patterns of seismic activity. Include events occurring during or near the time period represented in the staged MTA1 GNSS data (profiled temporal sample: December 3, 2024, approximately 00:00\u201301:24 UTC; full file temporal range not verified). Provide seismic activity context relevant to regional ground deformation monitoring, event-station distance relationships, and interpretation of GNSS displacement patterns in relation to tectonic activity.", "status": "completed", "execute": true, "source": "agent_next_expert", "parent_id": "analysis", "pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "provider_id": "", "model_id": "", "fallback_warnings": [], "stage": "delegate.completed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "return_to": "analysis", "depth": 0, "duration_ms": 16677, "execution_mode": "blueprint_chain_of_thought", "input": "Search for recent earthquake and seismic event catalog evidence within the Los Angeles region (center 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, radius 100 km). Report available event magnitudes, depths, epicenter locations, and temporal patterns of seismic activity. Include events occurring during or near the time period represented in the staged MTA1 GNSS data (profiled temporal sample: December 3, 2024, approximately 00:00\u201301:24 UTC; full file temporal range not verified). Provide seismic activity context relevant to regional ground deformation monitoring, event-station distance relationships, and interpretation of GNSS displacement patterns in relation to tectonic activity.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n(Delegating to seismic_event_catalog for earthquake/seismic event evidence; full analysis and synthesis pending.)\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": true, \"local_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"metadata_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"size_bytes\": 50424246, \"source_url\": \"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"status\": \"staged\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"completed_stages\": [\"geospatial\", \"data\"], \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 100, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"warnings\": [\"Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request\"]}, \"network_analysis\": {\"assessment\": \"MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence/duration not verified.\", \"network_context\": \"155 ranked stations available; MTA1 is closest; fallback stations (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km) enable multi-station analysis if needed\", \"station_id\": \"MTA1\", \"status\": \"preliminary_suitability_confirmed\"}, \"orchestrator_step\": \"delegating_to_analysis\", \"profile\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"scan_limited\": true, \"status\": \"complete\"}, \"request_type\": \"full_pipeline\", \"resource_candidate\": {\"geographically_grounded\": true, \"station_id\": \"MTA1\", \"status\": \"selected\"}, \"station_catalog\": {\"candidate_count\": 155, \"status\": \"ranked\"}, \"user_request_summary\": \"Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography...", "output": "**Seismic Event Catalog Capability Gap**\n\nThis analysis pack does not have a live earthquake event-catalog tool available for querying USGS, IRIS, or equivalent seismic databases. Therefore, the requested event-context evidence cannot be retrieved.\n\n**What is missing:**\nTo complete the event-context layer for the Los Angeles region (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, \u00b1100 km radius) during the December 3, 2024 time window, the workflow would require:\n- **USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API** or equivalent live event catalog query tool\n- **Event filtering by region, magnitude threshold, and date range**\n- **Magnitude, depth, epicenter coordinates, and temporal event data**\n- **Event-to-station distance calculations for MTA1 and network context**\n\n**Impact on Analysis:**\nWithout live event-catalog access, the synthesis cannot provide:\n- Recent seismic activity counts and magnitudes for the LA region\n- Event timing and epicenter context for GNSS displacement interpretation\n- Cross-correlation of GNSS observations with known seismic events\n- Event-driven deformation attribution\n\nThe staged MTA1 GNSS time-series and station network analysis remain complete and valid. Seismic event correlation would require a separate event-catalog query tool.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "completed_stages": ["geospatial", "data"], "event_context": {"blocker": "no live event catalog tool available in this pack", "limitations": ["no_live_event_catalog_tool"], "next_action": "add or call a live earthquake/event catalog tool (e.g., USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API) for event counts, magnitudes, depths, and dates", "status": "blocked", "verified_event_count": null}, "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "network_analysis": {"assessment": "MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence/duration not verified.", "network_context": "155 ranked stations available; MTA1 is closest; fallback stations (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km) enable multi-station analysis if needed", "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "preliminary_suitability_confirmed"}, "orchestrator_step": "delegating_to_analysis", "profile": {"path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "scan_limited": true, "status": "complete"}, "request_type": "full_pipeline", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected"}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 155, "status": "ranked"}, "user_request_summary": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact"}, "tools_called": [], "children": []}, {"agent_id": "analysis", "parent_id": "main", "dispatch_target": "analysis", "status": "completed", "stage": "parent.resumed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "resumed_from": "seismic_event_catalog", "depth": 0, "output": "**Seismic Event Catalog Capability Gap**\n\nThis analysis pack does not have a live earthquake event-catalog tool available for querying USGS, IRIS, or equivalent seismic databases. Therefore, the requested event-context evidence cannot be retrieved.\n\n**What is missing:**\nTo complete the event-context layer for the Los Angeles region (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, \u00b1100 km radius) during the December 3, 2024 time window, the workflow would require:\n- **USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API** or equivalent live event catalog query tool\n- **Event filtering by region, magnitude threshold, and date range**\n- **Magnitude, depth, epicenter coordinates, and temporal event data**\n- **Event-to-station distance calculations for MTA1 and network context**\n\n**Impact on Analysis:**\nWithout live event-catalog access, the synthesis cannot provide:\n- Recent seismic activity counts and magnitudes for the LA region\n- Event timing and epicenter context for GNSS displacement interpretation\n- Cross-correlation of GNSS observations with known seismic events\n- Event-driven deformation attribution\n\nThe staged MTA1 GNSS time-series and station network analysis remain complete and valid. Seismic event correlation would require a separate event-catalog query tool.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "completed_stages": ["geospatial", "data"], "event_context": {"blocker": "no live event catalog tool available in this pack", "limitations": ["no_live_event_catalog_tool"], "next_action": "add or call a live earthquake/event catalog tool (e.g., USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API) for event counts, magnitudes, depths, and dates", "status": "blocked", "verified_event_count": null}, "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "network_analysis": {"assessment": 