data: {"type": "semantic.event", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:45:53.025949+00:00", "payload": {"schema_version": "clio.semantic_event.v1", "event_id": "sem_2695ba23cf294efc", "event_type": "blueprint.delegation.parent_resumed", "session_id": "sess_57ac84d71ca3", "workspace_id": "ws_22a00fecef95", "trace_id": "trace_msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "span_id": "sem_2695ba23cf294efc", "parent_span_id": "", "status": "completed", "summary": "main resumed after analysis.", "live_observed": true, "detail_level": "semantic", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:45:53.011088+00:00", "actor": {"agent_id": "main", "role": "parent_expert"}, "subject": {"agent_id": "analysis", "role": "child_expert"}, "blueprint": {"pack_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "pack_version": "0.1.0", "agent_blueprint_id": "earthscope-gnss-region", "parent_expert": "main", "child_expert": "analysis"}, "provider": {}, "payload": {"agent_id": "main", "parent_id": "", "dispatch_target": "main", "status": "completed", "stage": "parent.resumed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "resumed_from": "analysis", "depth": 0, "output": "**MTA1 GNSS Station Analysis: Profile, Suitability, and Event-Context Summary**\n\n## GNSS Time-Series Profile\n\n**File & Data Structure:**\n- Staged CSV: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- Total rows: 250,000 | File size: 50.4 MB\n- All 8 required columns present: time (Unix ms), east, north, up (meters), sigEE, sigNN, sigUU (meters), qChannel (quality flag)\n\n**Displacement Ranges (profiled 5,000 rows):**\n- East: -0.07 to -0.03 m (mean: -0.047 m)\n- North: 0.029 to 0.058 m (mean: 0.045 m)\n- Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m (mean: 0.136 m)\n\n**Uncertainty Ranges (profiled 5,000 rows):**\n- Horizontal (sigEE/sigNN): 0.032\u20130.035 m (means: 3.3 cm)\n- Vertical (sigUU): 0.062\u20130.066 m (mean: 6.5 cm)\n\n**Temporal Coverage (profiled sample only):**\n- Time span: ~1.4 hours (December 3, 2024, 00:00\u201301:24 UTC)\n- Sample rows show 1000 ms increments (local 1 Hz sampling)\n- Null values in profiled rows: zero across all columns\n\n## Station Suitability Assessment\n\n**Geographic Position:**\nMTA1 is positioned 0.3 km from the Los Angeles region center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W), at the geographic heart of the analysis region. This central location is optimal for regional ground deformation monitoring.\n\n**Data Structure Fitness:**\nAll required GNSS analysis columns are present:\n- 3D displacement components (east, north, up)\n- 3D uncertainty components (sigEE, sigNN, sigUU)\n- Time reference for event correlation\n- Quality flag (qChannel, numeric, not decoded)\n\n**Preliminary Suitability Confirmation:**\nMTA1's central location and complete data structure support initial regional deformation context and seismic event station metadata analysis. A single station at the region center is a reasonable first-order choice for exploratory analysis.\n\n**Network Context:**\nMTA1 is the closest of 155 ranked EarthScope stations. Secondary candidates (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km, USC2 5.0 km, SILK 5.8 km) provide network redundancy and multi-station analysis options if scope expands.\n\n## Event-Context Capability Gap\n\n**Status:** Blocked \u2014 No live earthquake event-catalog tool available\n\nThe analysis pack lacks a live USGS/IRIS event-catalog query tool. Therefore, earthquake and seismic event evidence (magnitudes, depths, epicenter locations, temporal patterns) cannot be retrieved for the Los Angeles region.\n\n**Tools Needed for Complete Event Context:**\n- USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API or equivalent event-catalog service\n- Event filtering by region, magnitude, and date range\n- Event-to-station distance calculations for MTA1\n\n**Impact:** Without event-catalog access, the synthesis cannot cross-correlate GNSS observations with known seismic events or attribute deformation to specific earthquakes. The GNSS time-series and station analysis remain valid standalone evidence.\n\n## Critical Analysis Limitations\n\n**Scan-Limited Profile:**\nOnly 5,000 of 250,000 rows examined for statistics. Full-file cadence, duration, temporal continuity, and complete data-quality verification were not performed.\n\n**Unverified Full-File Characteristics:**\n- Full-file sampling cadence not confirmed (1 Hz observed in profiled sample)\n- Complete temporal span not verified\n- Missing-value status of full dataset not assessed\n- Quality flag (qChannel) not decoded\n\n**Conclusion:**\nPreliminary analysis of MTA1's suitability is supported by geographic position, column presence, and scan-limited uncertainty ranges. Complete suitability assessment and full-record quality verification require full-file analysis. Event-context correlation requires a live earthquake catalog tool.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "completed_stages": ["geospatial", "data"], "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "orchestrator_step": "delegating_to_analysis", "request_type": "full_pipeline", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected"}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 155, "status": "ranked"}, "user_request_summary": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact", "profile": {"status": "complete", "path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "scan_limited": true}, "network_analysis": {"assessment": "MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence/duration not verified.", "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "preliminary_suitability_confirmed", "network_context": "155 ranked stations available; MTA1 is closest; fallback stations (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km) enable multi-station analysis if needed"}, "event_context": {"blocker": "no live event catalog tool available in this pack", "limitations": ["no_live_event_catalog_tool"], "next_action": "add or call a live earthquake/event catalog tool (e.g., USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API) for event counts, magnitudes, depths, and dates", "status": "blocked", "verified_event_count": null}}}}}

event: message.part.added
id: 236
data: {"type": "message.part.added", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:45:53.026398+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "message_id": "msg_asst_b3567fb7ada5", "stream_source": "live", "part": {"id": "live_handoff_3e8fa393d966", "type": "expert_handoff", "metadata": {"agent_id": "main", "parent_id": "", "dispatch_target": "main", "status": "completed", "stage": "parent.resumed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "resumed_from": "analysis", "depth": 0, "output": "**MTA1 GNSS Station Analysis: Profile, Suitability, and Event-Context Summary**\n\n## GNSS Time-Series Profile\n\n**File & Data Structure:**\n- Staged CSV: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- Total rows: 250,000 | File size: 50.4 MB\n- All 8 required columns present: time (Unix ms), east, north, up (meters), sigEE, sigNN, sigUU (meters), qChannel (quality flag)\n\n**Displacement Ranges (profiled 5,000 rows):**\n- East: -0.07 to -0.03 m (mean: -0.047 m)\n- North: 0.029 to 0.058 m (mean: 0.045 m)\n- Up: 0.051 to 0.224 m (mean: 0.136 m)\n\n**Uncertainty Ranges (profiled 5,000 rows):**\n- Horizontal (sigEE/sigNN): 0.032\u20130.035 m (means: 3.3 cm)\n- Vertical (sigUU): 0.062\u20130.066 m (mean: 6.5 cm)\n\n**Temporal Coverage (profiled sample only):**\n- Time span: ~1.4 hours (December 3, 2024, 00:00\u201301:24 UTC)\n- Sample rows show 1000 ms increments (local 1 Hz sampling)\n- Null values in profiled rows: zero across all columns\n\n## Station Suitability Assessment\n\n**Geographic Position:**\nMTA1 is positioned 0.3 km from the Los Angeles region center (34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W), at the geographic heart of the analysis region. This central location is optimal for regional ground deformation monitoring.\n\n**Data Structure Fitness:**\nAll required GNSS analysis columns are present:\n- 3D displacement components (east, north, up)\n- 3D uncertainty components (sigEE, sigNN, sigUU)\n- Time reference for event correlation\n- Quality flag (qChannel, numeric, not decoded)\n\n**Preliminary Suitability Confirmation:**\nMTA1's central location and complete data structure support initial regional deformation context and seismic event station metadata analysis. A single station at the region center is a reasonable first-order choice for exploratory analysis.\n\n**Network Context:**\nMTA1 is the closest of 155 ranked EarthScope stations. Secondary candidates (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km, USC2 5.0 km, SILK 5.8 km) provide network redundancy and multi-station analysis options if scope expands.\n\n## Event-Context Capability Gap\n\n**Status:** Blocked \u2014 No live earthquake event-catalog tool available\n\nThe analysis pack lacks a live USGS/IRIS event-catalog query tool. Therefore, earthquake and seismic event evidence (magnitudes, depths, epicenter locations, temporal patterns) cannot be retrieved for the Los Angeles region.\n\n**Tools Needed for Complete Event Context:**\n- USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API or equivalent event-catalog service\n- Event filtering by region, magnitude, and date range\n- Event-to-station distance calculations for MTA1\n\n**Impact:** Without event-catalog access, the synthesis cannot cross-correlate GNSS observations with known seismic events or attribute deformation to specific earthquakes. The GNSS time-series and station analysis remain valid standalone evidence.\n\n## Critical Analysis Limitations\n\n**Scan-Limited Profile:**\nOnly 5,000 of 250,000 rows examined for statistics. Full-file cadence, duration, temporal continuity, and complete data-quality verification were not performed.\n\n**Unverified Full-File Characteristics:**\n- Full-file sampling cadence not confirmed (1 Hz observed in profiled sample)\n- Complete temporal span not verified\n- Missing-value status of full dataset not assessed\n- Quality flag (qChannel) not decoded\n\n**Conclusion:**\nPreliminary analysis of MTA1's suitability is supported by geographic position, column presence, and scan-limited uncertainty ranges. Complete suitability assessment and full-record quality verification require full-file analysis. Event-context correlation requires a live earthquake catalog tool.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "completed_stages": ["geospatial", "data"], "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "orchestrator_step": "delegating_to_analysis", "request_type": "full_pipeline", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected"}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 155, "status": "ranked"}, "user_request_summary": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact", "profile": {"status": "complete", "path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "scan_limited": true}, "network_analysis": {"assessment": "MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence/duration not verified.", "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "preliminary_suitability_confirmed", "network_context": "155 ranked stations available; MTA1 is closest; fallback stations (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km) enable multi-station analysis if needed"}, "event_context": {"blocker": "no live event catalog tool available in this pack", "limitations": ["no_live_event_catalog_tool"], "next_action": "add or call a live earthquake/event catalog tool (e.g., USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API) for event counts, magnitudes, depths, and dates", "status": "blocked", "verified_event_count": null}}, "stream_source": "live"}, "agent_id": "main", "text": "main resumed (from analysis)", "child_agent": "main", "stage": "parent.resumed", "status": "completed"}}}

