mporal span: ~1.4 hours (December 3, 2024)\n- Sample rate: ~1 Hz (1000 ms increments in profiled data)\n- Missing values: zero in profiled rows\n\n**Important Caveats:**\n- Plot shows 2,000 representative rows from 250,000-row file; not full-file coverage\n- Full-file cadence, duration, and completeness were not verified\n- Uncertainty bounds (sigEE, sigNN, sigUU) are present in CSV but not overlaid on plot lines\n- Time-series plot shows only the three displacement components; quality flag (qChannel) not displayed\n\n**Artifact Status:** Ready for discussion of regional GNSS deformation patterns at MTA1 station.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246, "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "status": "staged"}, "artifact": {"kind": "gnss_timeseries_plot", "path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png", "status": "ready", "columns": ["east", "north", "up"], "x_column": "time", "x_axis_kind": "epoch_milliseconds", "data_points_plotted": 2000, "total_rows_available": 250000, "title": "MTA1 GNSS Displacement Time-Series (Los Angeles Region, 0.3 km from center)"}, "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "completed_stages": ["geospatial", "data", "analysis", "visualization"], "event_context": {"blocker": "no live event catalog tool available in this pack", "limitations": ["no_live_event_catalog_tool"], "next_action": "add or call a live earthquake/event catalog tool (e.g., USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API) for event counts, magnitudes, depths, and dates", "status": "blocked", "verified_event_count": null}, "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "network_analysis": {"assessment": "MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cadence/duration not verified.", "network_context": "155 ranked stations available; MTA1 is closest; fallback stations (PKRD 2.2 km, ELSC 4.1 km) enable multi-station analysis if needed", "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "preliminary_suitability_confirmed"}, "orchestrator_step": "visualization_complete", "profile": {"columns": ["time", "east", "north", "up", "sigEE", "sigNN", "sigUU", "qChannel"], "path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "scan_limited": true, "status": "complete"}, "request_type": "full_pipeline", "resource_candidate": {"geographically_grounded": true, "station_id": "MTA1", "status": "selected"}, "station_catalog": {"candidate_count": 155, "status": "ranked"}, "user_request_summary": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact"}}}}

