th 0.029 to 0.058 m, up 0.051 to 0.224 m. Uncertainties: horizontal (sigEE/sigNN) mean ~0.033 m (3.3 cm), vertical (sigUU) mean ~0.065 m (6.5 cm). Zero null values in profiled rows.\n\n## Visualization\n- PNG artifact: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png`\n- Time-series plot of east, north, and up displacement components (2,000 data points plotted from 250,000-row file)\n- Title: \"MTA1 GNSS Displacement Time-Series (Los Angeles Region, 0.3 km from center)\"\n\n## Freshness, coverage & provenance limitations\n\n**Event-context gap:** This analysis pack has no live earthquake catalog tool (USGS/IRIS/equivalent). Seismic event counts, magnitudes, depths, epicenter locations, and temporal patterns for the LA region cannot be retrieved. GNSS observations cannot be cross-correlated with known seismic events.\n\n**Profile coverage:** Only 5,000 of 250,000 rows examined for min/max/mean statistics. Full-file temporal span, sampling cadence, and gap structure were not verified.\n\n**Plot coverage:** PNG displays 2,000 representative data points (subset of 250,000-row file). Complete temporal coverage not verified.\n\n**Uncertainty display:** sigEE/sigNN/sigUU uncertainty columns present in CSV but not graphically overlaid on displacement traces in the plot.\n\n**Quality flag:** qChannel numeric values present in CSV but not decoded or assessed; full-file data-quality interpretation not performed.\n\nAll paths, URLs, and numeric ranges copied verbatim from staged NDP resources.", "expert_handoffs": [], "tools_called": [], "file_diffs": [], "error_info": null, "reasoning": "The synthesis expert receives complete, grounded evidence from all four completed pipeline stages:\n\n1. **geospatial**: Resolved Los Angeles region with OSM Nominatim (center 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, 100 km radius)\n2. **data**: Staged MTA1 GNSS time-series CSV (50.4 MB, 250,000 rows, 8 columns, real source URL)\n3. **analysis**: Profiled CSV with scan-limited evidence (5,000 rows profiled, all required columns present, centimeter-scale uncertainties, zero nulls)\n4. **visualization**: Created PNG artifact (2,000 data points plotted, east/north/up displacement time-series)\n\n**Key grounded facts to extract and copy verbatim:**\n- Station ID: MTA1 (from `acquisition.local_path` filename token)\n- CSV path: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- Source URL: `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- PNG path: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png`\n- Data quality: analysis_ready=true, status=staged\n- Profile: rows_scanned=5000 (of 250000 total), status=complete\n- Artifact: status=ready\n- Resource candidate: station_id=MTA1, geographically_grounded=true, status=selected\n\n**Honest disclosures:**\n- Event-context blocker: no live USGS/earthquake catalog tool available\n- Scan-limited profile: cannot infer full-file cadence/duration/completeness from profiled sample\n- Plot limitation: 2,000 of 250,000 rows displayed; uncertainty bounds not overlaid\n\nThe final answer must be pure markdown prose with no JSON, no `workflow_state` blob, and no \"{\" character. All paths and URLs copied exactly as they appear upstream."}}}

