data: {"type": "message.part.added", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:48:51.279426+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "message_id": "msg_asst_b3567fb7ada5", "stream_source": "batch", "part": {"id": "part_42e4401dbfe1", "type": "thinking", "agent_id": "main", "text": "All pipeline stages have completed successfully:\n\n1. **geospatial** (\u2713): Los Angeles region resolved (center 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, 100 km radius, OSM Nominatim provenance)\n2. **data** (\u2713): MTA1 GNSS time-series CSV staged from NDP (50.4 MB, 250,000 rows)\n3. **analysis** (\u2713): CSV profiled, station suitability assessed (scan-limited to 5,000 rows, all 8 required columns present, centimeter-scale uncertainties)\n4. **visualization** (\u2713): PNG artifact created (2,000 data points, east/north/up displacement time-series)\n5. **synthesis** (\u2713): Final user-facing answer written with grounded evidence and honest limitations disclosed\n\nThe synthesis expert has merged all child evidence (geospatial resolution, staged data source, profile findings, PNG artifact path, event-context blocker) into a comprehensive markdown brief suitable for scientific discussion. Per system protocol, the orchestrator now finishes on the turn following synthesis completion, carrying its answer."}}}

event: message.part.completed
id: 295
data: {"type": "message.part.completed", "occurred_at": "2026-06-26T06:48:51.279443+00:00", "payload": {"turn_id": "msg_user_b0b5df728a09", "message_id": "msg_asst_b3567fb7ada5", "part_id": "part_61b1107fe477", "stream_source": "live", "final_text": "## Region\nLos Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States. Resolved center: 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W; search radius 100 km. Provenance: OpenStreetMap Nominatim geocoding (high confidence).\n\n## Station selected\nStation **MTA1** \u2014 located 0.3 km from region center. Sole station staged and analyzed, selected from 155 EarthScope candidates discovered within the region.\n\n## Data resource\n- Staged CSV: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- Source URL: `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- File size: 50.4 MB; total rows: 250,000\n\n## Profile evidence\nEight columns present: time (Unix milliseconds), displacement components east/north/up (meters), uncertainties sigEE/sigNN/sigUU (meters), quality flag qChannel. Profile scan-limited to 5,000 rows for statistics; full-file cadence and duration not verified. Displacement ranges (profiled sample): east \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m, north 0.029 to 0.058 m, up 0.051 to 0.224 m. Uncertainties: horizontal (sigEE/sigNN) mean ~0.033 m (3.3 cm), vertical (sigUU) mean ~0.065 m (6.5 cm). Zero null values in profiled rows.\n\n## Visualization\n- PNG artifact: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png`\n- Time-series plot of east, north, and up displacement components (2,000 data points plotted from 250,000-row file)\n- Title: \"MTA1 GNSS Displacement Time-Series (Los Angeles Region, 0.3 km from center)\"\n\n## Freshness, coverage & provenance limitations\n\n**Event-context gap:** This analysis pack has no live earthquake catalog tool (USGS/IRIS/equivalent). Seismic event counts, magnitudes, depths, epicenter locations, and temporal patterns for the LA region cannot be retrieved. GNSS observations cannot be cross-correlated with known seismic events.\n\n**Profile coverage:** Only 5,000 of 250,000 rows examined for min/max/mean statistics. Full-file temporal span, sampling cadence, and gap structure were not verified.\n\n**Plot coverage:** PNG displays 2,000 representative data points (subset of 250,000-row file). Complete temporal coverage not verified.\n\n**Uncertainty display:** sigEE/sigNN/sigUU uncertainty columns present in CSV but not graphically overlaid on displacement traces in the plot.\n\n**Quality flag:** qChannel numeric values present in CSV but not decoded or assessed; full-file data-quality interpretation not performed.\n\nAll paths, URLs, and numeric ranges copied verbatim from staged NDP resources."}}

