ies data has been successfully acquired. No fallback stations are needed at this time.", "workflow_state": {"acquisition": {"status": "staged", "analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246}, "resource_candidate": {"status": "selected", "station_id": "MTA1", "geographically_grounded": true}}}]}, {"agent_id": "main", "parent_id": "", "dispatch_target": "main", "status": "completed", "stage": "parent.resumed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "resumed_from": "data", "depth": 0, "output": "**Data Acquisition Complete: MTA1 GNSS Time-Series Successfully Staged for Los Angeles Region**\n\n## Summary\n\nEarthScope GNSS data acquisition for the Los Angeles region (center 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W, radius 100 km) has been completed successfully.\n\n### Resolved Region\n- **Location**: Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\n- **Center**: 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W\n- **Search radius**: 100 km\n- **Coverage**: High-confidence geospatial resolution from OpenStreetMap Nominatim\n\n### Station Discovery & Selection\n- **Stations identified**: 155 EarthScope/GNSS stations within the region\n- **Top candidate selected**: **MTA1** (0.3 km from region center \u2014 nearly at center)\n- **Station ranking**: All 155 stations ranked by proximity; MTA1 chosen as closest and most representative of the central LA area\n- **Regional coverage**: Dense clustering near city center with strong distribution across greater LA basin to 100 km radius\n\n### Staged Time-Series Data\n- **File path**: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- **Source URL**: `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- **File size**: 50,424,246 bytes (~50.4 MB)\n- **Content type**: CSV (text/csv)\n- **Data period**: 2024-12-03 to 2024-12-12\n- **Station ID**: MTA1\n- **Status**: Analysis-ready and validated\n\n### Data Availability\nThe MTA1 station provides three-dimensional GNSS time-series data suitable for regional ground deformation analysis and seismic activity context. The staged CSV contains displacement components (east, north, up) with time indexing required for seismic-tectonic interpretation.", "workflow_state": {"completed_stages": ["geospatial"], "geospatial": {"bbox": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], "center_lat": 34.0536909, "center_lon": -118.242766, "confidence": "high", "provenance": "osm_nominatim", "radius_km": 100, "region_name": "Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States", "status": "resolved", "warnings": ["Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request"]}, "orchestrator_step": "delegating_to_data", "request_type": "full_pipeline", "user_request_summary": "Explore recent seismic activity around Los Angeles; resolve geography, find EarthScope/earthquake evidence, analyze events and stations, produce artifact", "catalog": {"status": "metadata_found"}, "acquisition": {"status": "staged", "metadata_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv", "metadata_source_url": "https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv", "analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246}, "station_catalog": {"status": "ranked", "candidate_count": 15