ns present, centimeter-scale uncertainties, scan-limited evidence; (4) visualization PNG artifact created (2,000 points plotted) at artifact.path showing east/north/up displacement time-series for discussion of regional GNSS deformation patterns. Address the event-context blocker honestly: no live USGS/earthquake catalog tool available in this pack. Summarize limitations: scan-limited profile (5k of 250k rows), full-file cadence/duration not verified, uncertainty bounds present in CSV but not displayed in plot. Provide artifact path and source URLs as grounded evidence for discussion.\n\nParent evidence available for this delegated task:\n\n(Delegating to synthesis expert for final user-facing answer compilation.)\n\nAccumulated typed workflow state from prior CLIO tool evidence (authoritative; use this before local prose summaries):\n{\"workflow_state\": {\"acquisition\": {\"analysis_ready\": true, \"local_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"metadata_path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/earthscope_stations_clean.csv\", \"metadata_source_url\": \"https://nationaldataplatform.org/catalog/dataset/811f0bcc-99e5-455c-bcf6-7c63c2634f41/resource/a420cc30-2262-423a-8c63-3ad8d91f2a8f/download/earthscope_converted_data.csv\", \"size_bytes\": 50424246, \"source_url\": \"https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv\", \"status\": \"staged\"}, \"artifact\": {\"columns\": [\"east\", \"north\", \"up\"], \"data_points_plotted\": 2000, \"kind\": \"gnss_timeseries_plot\", \"path\": \"/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png\", \"status\": \"ready\", \"title\": \"MTA1 GNSS Displacement Time-Series (Los Angeles Region, 0.3 km from center)\", \"total_rows_available\": 250000, \"x_axis_kind\": \"epoch_milliseconds\", \"x_column\": \"time\"}, \"catalog\": {\"status\": \"metadata_found\"}, \"completed_stages\": [\"geospatial\", \"data\", \"analysis\", \"visualization\"], \"event_context\": {\"blocker\": \"no live event catalog tool available in this pack\", \"limitations\": [\"no_live_event_catalog_tool\"], \"next_action\": \"add or call a live earthquake/event catalog tool (e.g., USGS Earthquake Hazards Program API) for event counts, magnitudes, depths, and dates\", \"status\": \"blocked\", \"verified_event_count\": null}, \"geospatial\": {\"bbox\": [-118.6681798, 33.659541, -118.1552983, 34.337306], \"center_lat\": 34.0536909, \"center_lon\": -118.242766, \"confidence\": \"high\", \"provenance\": \"osm_nominatim\", \"radius_km\": 100, \"region_name\": \"Los Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"warnings\": [\"Default radius of 100 km assumed for regional GNSS station discovery and seismic event analysis; no explicit radius specified in user request\"]}, \"network_analysis\": {\"assessment\": \"MTA1 is geographically optimal at 0.3 km from region center with complete data structure for displacement analysis. Uncertainties in profiled sample are centimeter-scale (3.3 cm horizontal, 6.5 cm vertical). Profile is scan-limited; full-file cade...", "output": "## Region\nLos Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States. Resolved center: 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W; search radius 100 km. Provenance: OpenStreetMap Nominatim geocoding (high confidence).\n\n## Station selected\nStation **MTA1** \u2014 located 0.3 km from region center. Sole station staged and analyzed, selected from 155 EarthScope candidates discovered within the region.\n\n## Data resource\n- Staged CSV: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- Source URL: `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- File size: 50.4 MB; total rows: 250,000\n\n## Profile evidence\nEight columns present: time (Unix milliseconds), displacement components east/north/up (meters), uncertainties sigEE/sigNN/sigUU (meters), quality flag qChannel. Profile scan-limited to 5,000 rows for statistics; full-file cadence and duration not verified. Displacement ranges (profiled sample): east \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m, north 0.029 to 0.058 m, up 0.051 to 0.224 m. Uncertainties: horizontal (sigEE/sigNN) mean ~0.033 m (3.3 cm), vertical (sigUU) mean ~0.065 m (6.5 cm). Zero null values in profiled rows.\n\n## Visualization\n- PNG artifact: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png`\n- Time-series plot of east, north, and up displacement components (2,000 data points plotted from 250,000-row file)\n- Title: \"MTA1 GNSS Displacement Time-Series (Los Angeles Region, 0.3 km from center)\"\n\n## Freshness, coverage & provenance limitations\n\n**Event-context gap:** This analysis pack has no live earthquake catalog tool (USGS/IRIS/equivalent). Seismic event counts, magnitudes, depths, epicenter locations, and temporal patterns for the LA region cannot be retrieved. GNSS observations cannot be cross-correlated with known seismic events.\n\n**Profile coverage:** Only 5,000 of 250,000 rows examined for min/max/mean statistics. Full-file temporal span, sampling cadence, and gap structure were not verified.\n\n**Plot coverage:** PNG displays 2,000 representative data points (subset of 250,000-row file). Complete temporal coverage not verified.\n\n**Uncertainty display:** sigEE/sigNN/sigUU uncertainty columns present in CSV but not graphically overlaid on displacement traces in the plot.\n\n**Quality flag:** qChannel numeric values present in CSV but not decoded or assessed; full-file data-quality interpretation not performed.\n\nAll paths, URLs, and numeric ranges copied verbatim from staged NDP resources.", "workflow_state": {"resource_candidate": {"status": "selected", "station_id": "MTA1", "geographically_grounded": true}, "acquisition": {"status": "staged", "analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246}, "profile": {"status": "complete", "rows_scanned": 5000}, "artifact": {"status": "ready", "path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png"}}, "tools_called": [], "children": []}, {"agent_id": "main", "parent_id": "", "dispatch_target": "main", "status": "completed", "stage": "parent.resumed", "delegation_lifecycle": "sync", "resumed_from": "synthesis", "depth": 0, "output": "## Region\nLos Angeles, Los Angeles County, California, United States. Resolved center: 34.0536909\u00b0N, -118.242766\u00b0W; search radius 100 km. Provenance: OpenStreetMap Nominatim geocoding (high confidence).\n\n## Station selected\nStation **MTA1** \u2014 located 0.3 km from region center. Sole station staged and analyzed, selected from 155 EarthScope candidates discovered within the region.\n\n## Data resource\n- Staged CSV: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- Source URL: `https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv`\n- File size: 50.4 MB; total rows: 250,000\n\n## Profile evidence\nEight columns present: time (Unix milliseconds), displacement components east/north/up (meters), uncertainties sigEE/sigNN/sigUU (meters), quality flag qChannel. Profile scan-limited to 5,000 rows for statistics; full-file cadence and duration not verified. Displacement ranges (profiled sample): east \u22120.07 to \u22120.03 m, north 0.029 to 0.058 m, up 0.051 to 0.224 m. Uncertainties: horizontal (sigEE/sigNN) mean ~0.033 m (3.3 cm), vertical (sigUU) mean ~0.065 m (6.5 cm). Zero null values in profiled rows.\n\n## Visualization\n- PNG artifact: `/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1_displacement_timeseries.png`\n- Time-series plot of east, north, and up displacement components (2,000 data points plotted from 250,000-row file)\n- Title: \"MTA1 GNSS Displacement Time-Series (Los Angeles Region, 0.3 km from center)\"\n\n## Freshness, coverage & provenance limitations\n\n**Event-context gap:** This analysis pack has no live earthquake catalog tool (USGS/IRIS/equivalent). Seismic event counts, magnitudes, depths, epicenter locations, and temporal patterns for the LA region cannot be retrieved. GNSS observations cannot be cross-correlated with known seismic events.\n\n**Profile coverage:** Only 5,000 of 250,000 rows examined for min/max/mean statistics. Full-file temporal span, sampling cadence, and gap structure were not verified.\n\n**Plot coverage:** PNG displays 2,000 representative data points (subset of 250,000-row file). Complete temporal coverage not verified.\n\n**Uncertainty display:** sigEE/sigNN/sigUU uncertainty columns present in CSV but not graphically overlaid on displacement traces in the plot.\n\n**Quality flag:** qChannel numeric values present in CSV but not decoded or assessed; full-file data-quality interpretation not performed.\n\nAll paths, URLs, and numeric ranges copied verbatim from staged NDP resources.", "workflow_state": {"resource_candidate": {"status": "selected", "station_id": "MTA1", "geographically_grounded": true}, "acquisition": {"status": "staged", "analysis_ready": true, "local_path": "/tmp/claude-1000/-home-jcernuda/bb1bd9e8-d4b5-42a4-b525-af9e6ee77aaa/scratchpad/la_run/ws/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "source_url": "https://ds2.datacollaboratory.org/Earthscope_api_dec2024/raw_csv/MTA1.CI.LY_.30.csv", "size_bytes": 50424246}, "profile": {"status": "complete", "rows_scanned": 5000}, "artifact": {"status": "ready", "path": "/tmp/cl